  "id": "COMPOUND:16658 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "Hexacosyl Hexadecanoate is shown to interact with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, a key enzyme involved in cellular signaling and homeostasis. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including Hexacosyl Hexadecanoate, which appears to modulate its activity in prostate cells. The evidence suggests that Hexacosyl Hexadecanoate may influence the signaling pathways of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, potentially affecting cellular processes in prostate cells. The presence of multiple targets, including both well-characterized compounds and direct interactions with prostate cells, supports a mechanistic link between Hexacosyl Hexadecanoate and prostate cell function. The observed effects on prostate cells are consistent with a role in cellular regulation, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
